3. INVENTORY MODULE
   (bridal dresses, rental outfits, accessories — ledger, balances, valuation)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------


    -- QUANTITY MODEL  (ADR-004) — four numbers, one ledger, one reservations table:
    --   on_hand_qty   = Σ ledger quantity            → physically in the warehouse
    --   on_rent_qty   = Σ rent_out − Σ rent_return   → out with customers
    --   owned_qty     = on_hand_qty + on_rent_qty    → what the shop OWNS  ← VALUATION
    --   reserved_qty  = Σ active reservations        → NOT from the ledger
    --   available_qty = on_hand_qty − reserved_qty   → sellable / bookable today
    --
    -- A dress at a wedding is still an asset: stock worth uses owned_qty.
    -- Reservations are NOT stock movements — 'reserve'/'release' do not exist.
    --
    -- COSTING (ADR-001) — Weighted Average Cost per (item, warehouse):
    --   stock-in : new_avg = (on_hand×avg + qty_in×landed_unit_cost)/(on_hand+qty_in)
    --   stock-out: snapshot current avg onto the transaction; avg unchanged
    --
    -- Stock-in  paths: procurement receipt · manual entry · sale return restock · transfer in
    -- Stock-out paths: sale complete · dispose · supplier return · transfer out
    -- Rental    paths: rent_out (leaves shop) · rent_return (comes back)


